. The edition has only two such bars (45 and 46). Bar 47 is slurred C#4–D4 quarters, which this figure does not match. So the third figure is either a bar the copyist has that the edition doesn't, or I'm misreading the faint image. Either way, the line clearly goes past bar 45 and includes at least bar 46.","right":false,"insights":"The copyist shortens nearly everything: stroked notes for repeated 8ths, and a repeat sign for the 16th figure. That leaves few real pitches to compare, and a third copy of the figure doesn't line up with the edition. A higher-resolution image with clear barlines, or a note in the edition saying where the copyist repeats bars, would make this easy to decide."},"ttft_ms":13577,"type":"result","duration_ms":38668,"uuid":"7c3572c3-2fdc-4b8c-b875-5dd6d8b4e797","ttft_stream_ms":1599,"time_to_request_ms":334,"first_content_frame_ms":1599,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":4,"outputTokens":3122,"cacheReadInputTokens":1046,"cacheCreationInputTokens":10073,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.1432492,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":2498,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":10073,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}}}
